---
import DocPage from '../components/ui/DocPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
import { CONTACTS } from '../data/operator';
---

<DocPage
  eyebrow="Accessibility"
  title="Accessibility"
  pageTitle={`Accessibility: ${SITE.fullName}`}
  description="Reelay's accessibility statement for this website and the app: what we aim for, what we check, what we know isn't right yet, and how to tell us."
  updated="October 12, 2026"
>
  <Fragment slot="lede">We want Reelay and this website to work for everyone. <strong>This is what we aim for, what we check, and how to tell us when we miss.</strong></Fragment>

  <section id="website">
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>We aim for WCAG 2.2 at level AA. In particular:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Text meets AA contrast in both the light and the dark look; the colour pairs are checked automatically on every build.</li>
      <li>Everything works with a keyboard, with a visible focus ring and a “Skip to content” link. Tabs follow the usual arrow-key pattern.</li>
      <li>The site follows your system’s light or dark setting and honours “Reduce motion”: nothing moves, fades or tilts when it’s on.</li>
      <li>Nothing plays by itself. Demo videos are muted, captioned, and have play and pause controls.</li>
      <li>Product illustrations have text descriptions, and tables are real tables.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="app">
    <h2>The Reelay app</h2>
    <p>Reelay is a native Mac app built with Qt. It has Light, Dark and Black themes, and builds Custom themes from a profile’s colours while keeping text readable whatever colours are chosen. Every control has a plain-language tip, and the player works from the keyboard (Space or K, J and L, the arrow keys, M).</p>
  </section>

  <section id="known">
    <h2>What we know isn’t right yet</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Some product illustrations on this site are detailed pictures of the app; their descriptions summarise them rather than list every element.</li>
      <li>We haven’t yet completed a full VoiceOver review of the app.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2>Tell us</h2>
    <p>If something on this site or in Reelay doesn’t work for you, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACTS.support}`}>{CONTACTS.support}</a> with the page or screen and what happened. We reply within five working days.</p>
  </section>
</DocPage>
